+## M5 - Streamlit presentation dashboard and reproducibility (2026-11-22)
+
+- Staged presentation navigation and shared state: Organize the Streamlit app into
+  six synchronized views (`overview`, `m1`, `m2`, `m3`, `m4`, `pipeline`) backed by
+  `presentation.py`, `presentation.css`, `presentation_views.py`, and session-local
+  memoization (`memo`), so active preset or schedule choices propagate across all
+  four modules without leaking stale live-CBC results after input changes.
+- Clean-clone startup and offline bundle: `run_all.py --stage m5` calls
+  `app.precompute.run_m5` to verify M1–M4 invariants and deterministically emit
+  `app/m5_bundle.json` (sorted keys, 6-decimal rounding, no timestamps) without
+  mutating M1–M4 directories. Full-dataset mode uses `app/m5_bundle.json` when seed
+  and dataset SHA-256 match, falling back transparently to repository artifacts.
+- Bounded live solves and strict upload validation: Restrict interactive CBC solves
+  to slices and uploaded CSVs under configurable `time_limit`, enforcing size caps
+  (512 KiB / 2,000 rows / 150 staff / 150 sessions / 120 days / 15,000 overlap
+  pairs; 5,000 staff-day cells for live DFA constraints; 2 MiB schedule uploads).
+- Slice calibration fallback: Pooled lag-one OLS in M4 needs at least two weekly
+  blocks; single-day `toy` or short slices reuse the 27-day Faculty baseline
+  parameters `(a, b, r)` and threshold `H` and label the calibration source.
+
